WEBVTT

00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.170
This is the MAID Accountability Report.

00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:07.250
What you're about to hear are facts — sourced entirely from Health Canada's own publications.

00:00:07.250 --> 00:00:12.840
In 2016, one thousand and eighteen Canadians died under Medical Assistance in Dying.

00:00:12.840 --> 00:00:14.306
By 2024?

00:00:14.306 --> 00:00:18.795
That number had risen to sixteen thousand, two hundred and sixty-five.

00:00:18.795 --> 00:00:20.806
That is not a gradual increase.

00:00:20.806 --> 00:00:22.818
That is an acceleration.

00:00:22.818 --> 00:00:24.534
Let me put that in perspective.

00:00:24.534 --> 00:00:32.488
The Netherlands — the country that pioneered legal euthanasia in 2002 — took twenty years to reach four point eight percent of all deaths.

00:00:32.488 --> 00:00:35.386
Canada matched that rate... in just seven years.

00:00:35.386 --> 00:00:40.465
Five point zero five percent of all Canadian deaths in 2024 were MAID deaths.

00:00:40.465 --> 00:00:45.999
One in every nineteen point eight people who died in Canada... died by government-administered lethal injection.

00:00:45.999 --> 00:00:52.897
Veterans have testified — under oath, before Parliamentary committee — that Veterans Affairs caseworkers offered them MAID.

00:00:52.897 --> 00:00:54.874
During calls about wheelchair ramps.

00:00:54.874 --> 00:00:56.795
During calls about housing support.

00:00:56.795 --> 00:00:58.409
At least five veterans.

00:00:58.409 --> 00:00:59.420
On the record.

00:00:59.420 --> 00:01:07.113
A fifty-one year old Ontario woman with Multiple Chemical Sensitivities chose MAID after years of being unable to find affordable housing.

00:01:07.113 --> 00:01:11.454
She told journalists — and I quote — the government sees me as expendable.

00:01:11.454 --> 00:01:14.749
There is no independent oversight body for MAID in Canada.

00:01:14.749 --> 00:01:16.272
Doctors self-report.

00:01:16.272 --> 00:01:19.147
The Auditor General has never audited the program.

00:01:19.147 --> 00:01:23.738
Three consecutive RCMP Commissioners have launched zero investigations.

00:01:23.738 --> 00:01:29.318
The United Nations Special Rapporteur on the Rights of Persons with Disabilities has formally raised concerns.

00:01:29.318 --> 00:01:34.715
The UN Human Rights Committee flagged Canada's MAID regime in their 2023 Periodic Review.

00:01:34.715 --> 00:01:36.238
The world is watching.
